verses.text:
Jerusalem lay empty, like a wilderness;
none of her children went in or out.
The sanctuary was trampled down,
and foreigners held the citadel;
it had become a lodging place for the Gentiles.
Joy was taken away from Jacob;
the flute and the lyre fell silent.

"The flesh of your devoted ones they scattered,
and around Jerusalem they spilled their blood,
and none was there to bury them."{h}

The land was at rest all the days of Simon.
He sought the good of his nation;
his rule and his glory pleased them all his days.

In peace they worked their fields;
the soil yielded its harvest,
and the orchards of the plain bore fruit.

He gave strength to all the lowly of his people;
he searched out the law
and did away with every lawless and wicked person.
